WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.180
Luke 17

00:02.180 --> 00:05.480
And he said to his disciples,

00:06.540 --> 00:11.680
Temptations to sin are sure to come, but woe to the one through whom they come.

00:12.240 --> 00:15.880
It would be better for him if a millstone were hung around his neck,

00:16.100 --> 00:21.660
and he were cast into the sea, than that he should cause one of these little ones to sin.

00:22.580 --> 00:29.860
Pay attention to yourselves. If your brother sins, rebuke him, and if he repents, forgive him.

00:30.340 --> 00:35.460
And if he sins against you seven times in the day, and turns to you seven times, saying,

00:35.840 --> 00:38.740
I repent, you must forgive him.

00:39.440 --> 00:40.980
The apostles said to the Lord,

00:41.700 --> 00:43.780
Increase our faith.

00:44.280 --> 00:45.720
And the Lord said,

00:45.960 --> 00:51.240
If you had faith like a grain of mustard seed, you could say to this mulberry tree,

00:51.780 --> 00:55.880
Be uprooted and planted in the sea, and it would obey you.

00:57.100 --> 00:59.820
Will any one of you who has a servant plowing or

00:59.820 --> 00:59.980
keeping a millstone, or a millstone plowing, or a millstone plowing, or a millstone plowing,

00:59.980 --> 01:02.660
say to him when he has come in from the field,

01:03.200 --> 01:05.640
Come at once and recline at table.

01:06.480 --> 01:07.780
Will he not rather say to him,

01:08.320 --> 01:12.400
Prepare supper for me, and dress properly, and serve me while I eat and drink,

01:12.720 --> 01:15.240
and afterward you will eat and drink?

01:15.900 --> 01:18.520
Does he thank the servant because he did what was commanded?

01:19.300 --> 01:23.040
So you also, when you have done all that you were commanded, say,

01:23.680 --> 01:27.960
We are unworthy servants. We have only done what was our duty.

01:29.980 --> 01:34.380
On the way to Jerusalem, he was passing along between Samaria and Galilee.

01:34.940 --> 01:38.360
And as he entered a village, he was met by ten lepers,

01:38.360 --> 01:41.400
who stood at a distance and lifted up their voices, saying,

01:42.160 --> 01:48.760
Jesus, Master, have mercy on us.

01:49.520 --> 01:51.060
When he saw them, he said to them,

01:51.760 --> 01:54.760
Go, and show yourselves to the priests.

01:55.640 --> 01:57.440
And as they went, they were cleansed.

01:58.080 --> 01:59.960
Then one of them, when he saw that he was cleansed,

01:59.960 --> 02:02.960
was healed, turned back, praising God with a loud voice.

02:03.280 --> 02:06.700
And he fell on his face at Jesus' feet, giving him thanks.

02:07.440 --> 02:08.760
Now he was a Samaritan.

02:09.520 --> 02:10.540
Then Jesus answered,

02:11.040 --> 02:13.840
Were not ten cleansed? Where are the nine?

02:14.780 --> 02:18.780
Was no one found to return and give praise to God except this foreigner?

02:19.380 --> 02:20.660
And he said to him,

02:21.440 --> 02:25.800
Rise, and go your way. Your faith has made you well.

02:27.640 --> 02:29.940
Being asked by the Pharisees when the kingdom was made,

02:29.960 --> 02:31.060
the kingdom of God would come.

02:31.640 --> 02:32.520
He answered them,

02:33.280 --> 02:36.640
The kingdom of God is not coming with signs to be observed,

02:37.160 --> 02:40.540
nor will they say, Look, here it is, or there.

02:41.560 --> 02:45.660
For behold, the kingdom of God is in the midst of you.

02:46.380 --> 02:47.800
And he said to the disciples,

02:48.740 --> 02:53.420
The days are coming when you will desire to see one of the days of the Son of Man,

02:53.640 --> 02:55.200
and you will not see it.

02:55.560 --> 02:58.660
And they will say to you, Look there, or look here.

02:58.880 --> 02:59.940
Do not go out.

02:59.960 --> 03:00.840
Do not go out or follow them.

03:01.840 --> 03:06.200
For as the lightning flashes and lights up the sky from one side to the other,

03:06.740 --> 03:09.260
so will the Son of Man be in his day.

03:10.480 --> 03:15.540
But first, he must suffer many things and be rejected by this generation.

03:16.540 --> 03:21.280
Just as it was in the days of Noah, so will it be in the days of the Son of Man.

03:22.020 --> 03:26.140
They were eating and drinking and marrying and being given in marriage,

03:26.480 --> 03:29.080
until the day when Noah entered the ark,

03:29.080 --> 03:32.160
and the flood came and destroyed them all.

03:33.280 --> 03:36.400
Likewise, just as it was in the days of Lot,

03:36.720 --> 03:40.360
they were eating and drinking, buying and selling, planting and building.

03:40.980 --> 03:43.520
But on the day when Lot went out from Sodom,

03:43.980 --> 03:47.480
fire and sulfur rained from heaven and destroyed them all.

03:48.180 --> 03:52.000
So will it be on the day when the Son of Man is revealed.

03:52.660 --> 03:57.260
On that day, let the one who is on the housetop with his goods in the house

03:57.260 --> 03:58.960
not come down to take them.

03:58.960 --> 04:03.900
And likewise, let the one who is in the field not turn back.

04:04.580 --> 04:06.040
Remember Lot's wife.

04:07.420 --> 04:10.640
Whoever seeks to preserve his life will lose it,

04:11.020 --> 04:13.540
but whoever loses his life will keep it.

04:14.120 --> 04:17.080
I tell you, in that night there will be two in one bed.

04:17.520 --> 04:19.620
One will be taken and the other left.

04:20.440 --> 04:22.560
There will be two women grinding together.

04:23.000 --> 04:25.900
One will be taken and the other left.

04:26.800 --> 04:28.020
And they said to him,

04:28.060 --> 04:28.940
Where?

04:28.980 --> 04:29.480
There, Lord.

04:30.280 --> 04:31.180
He said to them,

04:31.940 --> 04:35.480
Where the corpse is, there the vultures will gather.

